he empty-map path (reverting the parser to a plain `{}` map still fails the `getPrototypeOf(...) === null` assertion), but a regression specifically in handling of a *genuinely* `__proto__`-keyed JSON document would sail through — which materially changes what an engineer editing the parser or adding cases should do (e.g., use a raw string body). This survives.\n\nSTEP 2 — emit:\n\n```atlas-fact\n{\"claim\": \"Despite its name, the POLICY-proto-1 test never actually writes a __proto__ key into policy.json: the object literal { __proto__: ['seat:x'] } sets the prototype instead of creating an own property, so JSON.stringify serializes the scopes as {} and the test exercises an empty scopes map rather than a __proto__-keyed one.\"}\n```"